  "note": "Synthetic Humbling Draught gains 2 life, strips target creature's abilities until end of turn, then gains 3, all in one resolution. Aimed at Ajani's Pridemate, the first gain finds the ability and the second does not (CR 603.10: a trigger looks at the game as the event happened), so alice gains the same 5 and the Pridemate takes one counter. The Haskell test read the Pridemate's triggered abilities off the projection; here Radiant Fountain's later gain of 2 that turn leaves it on one counter, the strip lasting until end of turn. Twin of the control that aims at the Goblin Piker and leaves two counters. Synthetic because every printing that strips abilities and does more in one resolution strips first (Day of Black Sun, Snakeform), and the three that order it the other way need a condition the engine lacks (Merfolk Trickster, The Wondrous Wasp, Tishana's Tidebinder).",
